  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlas Air obligated $480M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Atlas Air recorded 263 awards during the same period, with an average award size of $1.8M. Atlas Air obligations are down 36.8% year over year. Atlas Air has an uneven multi-year record: FY21 obligations were $13.5M, FY22 obligations were $1.7M, FY23 obligations were $6M, FY24 obligations were $3.7M, and FY25 obligations were $759M. Atlas Air work in FY2026 to date concentrates in a small set of NAICS markets. Atlas Air recorded $479M in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation, which dominates the FY2026 to date total. Atlas Air also reported smaller amounts in related markets: $333K in Other Technical and Trade Schools, $332K in Flight Training, and $268K in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation. Atlas Air current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. Atlas Air award-value tables show total contract values for the largest awards and expiring contracts separate from the contract obligation figures presented here.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Atlas Air obligations by market?",
        "body": "Atlas Air obligations are highly concentrated in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation, which accounted for $479M of FY2026 to date obligations. Atlas Air obligations in the next-largest NAICS markets are much smaller: $333K in Other Technical and Trade Schools, $332K in Flight Training, and $268K in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Atlas Air trended across recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Atlas Air obligations rose and fell across the period shown. Atlas Air obligations were $13.5M in FY21, $1.7M in FY22, $6M in FY23, $3.7M in FY24, $759M in FY25, and $480M in FY26 to date, representing a year-over-year change down 36.8%."
      }
    ]
